EF AI Workspace (#198): sidebar v3, owner-approved 2026-10-25 («اعتمد ونفذ بدقة») after two notes on v2: the collapsed
sidebar kept the old order, and Projects, Skills and Documents replaced the chats inside the sidebar.

- Pages in the main area (UnifiedSidebar/efSidebar.ts, hooks/Nav/useUnifiedSidebarLinks.ts, routes/index.tsx,
  components/EfPages/): Projects (upstream /projects), Skills, Documents, memory, bookmarks and ready commands (prompts)
  open as pages; /files, /memories, /bookmarks and /prompts are new routes, /skills and /prompts/:id gain the list beside
  the detail (EfSectionPage: title, menu button on phones, list and detail side by side or one at a time on phones). The
  sidebar keeps the chat search and history; the open page's row is aria-current. The agent builder and the parameters
  (admins, bound to the open chat) stay panels; opening a page puts them away. A section remembered as the v2 panel
  falls back to the chats.
- Column (UnifiedSidebar/EfSidebarColumn.tsx): page rows are links (new tab on modified clicks); on a phone a row closes
  the drawer, then opens its page. The dead Projects panel (EfProjectsPanel.tsx, ProjectsSection `embedded`) is gone.
- Collapsed rail (UnifiedSidebar/ExpandedPanel.tsx): toggle, «New chat», «Search» (opens the column with the cursor in
  the chat search), a line, Projects, Skills, Documents, «More» (an Ariakit menu beside the rail: memory, bookmarks, ready
  commands and any other section; for admins the marketplace, the builder and the parameters under «Admins only»), the
  account. The hidden shortcut targets (mobile/ShortcutTargets.tsx, now with the open page pressed) keep the panel
  shortcuts working from the column and the rail.
- Documents (SidePanel/Files/PanelTable.tsx `onAttached`, EfPages/EfFilesPage.tsx): choosing a document attaches it to
  the open chat, as the files panel did, records it in that chat's composer draft (the composer restores attachments
  from its draft when it mounts) and goes back to the chat.
- List panels as pages (Prompts/sidebar/GroupSidePanel.tsx, Skills/sidebar/SkillsSidePanel.tsx): visible whenever mounted,
  so they load their next pages whatever the sidebar does. The page header carries the phone's menu button
  (Skills/layouts/SkillsView.tsx, Prompts/forms/PromptForm.tsx). A prompt's copy button sits on the end side with room
  for it (Prompts/display/PromptTextCard.tsx). Project chats get row and cell roles under their grid
  (Projects/ProjectChatList.tsx, axe aria-required-children).

